Task: Concurrency Architecture Recommendation for Log Processing Pipeline
Repo: github.com/cli/logtail, File: `pkg/pipeline/processor.go`

Current implementation is synchronous:
```go
type Processor struct {
    handlers []Handler
}
func (p *Processor) Process(lines <-chan string) {
    for line := range lines { p.handle(line) }
}
```

Requirements:
Evaluate three concurrency models for processing high-throughput CLI log streams (up to 50k lines/sec): worker pools with fixed channels, dynamic goroutines with semaphores, and x/sync/errgroup. Compare memory footprint, backpressure handling, and error propagation under load. Provide a written architecture decision record (ADR) with a recommended design.
